{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"],"title":"Type Properties"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"title":"SegmentStore","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentStore.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L61"},"modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStore","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"code":["let store = try SegmentStore(events: [SignedUp.self, CheckedOut.self])","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","isActive":true},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Only events of the types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and produce no drop report, but are lost if the app ends first.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record’s context is not kept: a recovered record is in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as its span ended with the earlier run.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}]},{"text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A segment kept for one undelivered","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record keeps its delivered ones too. Only recovery rewrites a segment: one still holding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records after it drops some (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The log never holds more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"type":"text","text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered yields a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A record too large for an empty log"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is kept in memory only."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Recovery.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"code":"isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Other versions."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changed event types.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional one added since is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stored at another ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event.schemaVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/directory":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the store keeps its segments."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"directory","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"directory"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","text":"FilePath"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/directory"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"title":"DropReport","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"size, until they are delivered."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"title":"SegmentStore","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"writeFailed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"recordCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"timestamps","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ClosedRange","preciseIdentifier":"s:SN","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Date","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"title":"DropReport.writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/writefailed(recordcount:timestamps:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","abstract":[{"text":"Writing ","type":"text"},{"code":"recordCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" records, tracked within ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamps","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", to disk failed (the disk is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, say, or segments that couldn’t be deleted fill the bound), so they are kept in memory","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only: delivered in this run if it lasts long","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"enough, lost if it ends first.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"versionMismatch"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"event"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"storedVersion"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"currentVersion"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"recordCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"DropReport.versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport\/versionmismatch(event:storedversion:currentversion:recordcount:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordCount"},{"type":"text","text":" intact records of the event named "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"},{"type":"text","text":" stored at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"storedVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", while the store’s type of that name is at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"currentVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":"), and dropped them without decoding them: the version changed for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change their bytes can’t be read through. Reported once per segment, or per database, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each event and stored version, by the event’s name and then the stored version."}]},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RecordStore","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://